Working with customers pursuing personalisation at scale, an optimal content supply chain is a necessity.&nbsp; With the emergence of generative AI and its potential to supercharge the supply of hyper personalised&nbsp; content we are seeking a Senior Content Supply Consultant to help customers assess, optimise and manage their content supply processes, delivering content seamlessly and&nbsp; efficiently to execute outstanding consumer experiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

WHAT YOU’LL DO&nbsp;

• Lead inspiring business discovery workstreams and align with customers on relevant business&nbsp; goals and critical metrics&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Map the content lifecycle from creation to distribution, including all stages and touchpoints.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Assess the customer’s content supply process to identify inefficiencies and bottlenecks&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Define the role of Generative AI and automation capabilities to reduce cost and time to create,&nbsp; produce and deliver content&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Perform complex process re-design to align the content supply process to a customer’s strategy&nbsp; and drive dramatic improvements in productivity, cycle time, quality, and customer satisfaction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Define workflows to outline the sequence of tasks, responsibilities, dependencies, and approvals&nbsp; required to move content from one stage to the next.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Guide customers to train AI models on data to ensure a consistent and aligned brand representation across channels&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Help customers to assess current brand guidelines and define AI integration objectives, develop&nbsp; AI-specific guidelines, train the team and implement monitoring and evaluation processes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Design effective content approval processes to ensure published content aligns with a customer’s&nbsp; policies and expectations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Develop the implementation strategy &amp; roadmap in partnership with Technical Architects and customer teams for Adobe solutions that enable content supply, e.g. Adobe Experience Manager,&nbsp; Workfront, Creative Cloud, Express, Frame.io etc&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Research and define relevant content performance and content process benchmarks&nbsp;

• Design and implement content performance and content process reporting mechanisms to&nbsp; monitor progress against KPIs&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Analyse performance and surface insights informing continued optimisation and validating&nbsp; business outcomes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Perform organisational analysis to assess barriers to adoption and develop mitigation strategies.&nbsp; Advise and lead customers through the change required to adopt optimised content tools and&nbsp; processes across the customer org and involved 3rd parties&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Identify and enable customers teams on the required capability, functionality and features across&nbsp; Adobe technologies that facilitate content supply requirements with a specialist focus on Adobe&nbsp; Experience Manager and Workfront&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Support the enablement of customer teams across roles, responsibilities and process that&nbsp; facilitate the customer’s optimised content supply chain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Continually grow your footprint and role within the client engagement and relationship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

